<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Maria I della Rovere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/della-rovere">Della Rovere</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Maria I della Rovere was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>, who arranged his adoption by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guidobaldo-da-montefeltro">Guidobaldo da Montefeltro</a>. He inherited the Duchy of Urbino in 1508 and received Pesaro in 1512. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-x">Pope Leo X</a> drove him out in 1516, but he recovered the duchy in 1521, made Pesaro his main residence and commanded the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-i-della-rovere.jpg" alt="Francesco Maria I della Rovere" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Francesco_Maria_della_Rovere,_Duke_of_Urbino_(by_Titian)_%E2%80%93_Galleria_degli_Uffizi,_Florence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1508 the duchy passed to <b>Francesco Maria I della Rovere</b>, nephew of Pope Julius II, and from 1523 Pesaro became the main residence.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-urbino">Duchy of Urbino</a></li><li><blockquote>After Giovanni's son died young, Pope Julius II granted Pesaro in 1512 to his nephew <b>Francesco Maria I della Rovere</b>, joining it to the Duchy of Urbino.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-pesaro">Lordship of Pesaro</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-gallica">Senigallia</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Pesaro, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.71,13.22&amp;year=1521" aria-label="Senigallia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4868 614 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Francesco Maria I della Rovere"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5318 884h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5318 884h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.71,13.22&amp;year=1521">What was here in 1521? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
